From 1c8c88fa9177addeeaaedee8d0a8a3ab882d7075 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:11:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] volume_manager: Fix missing <algorithm> include for
 std::replace

PublicVolume.cpp uses std::replace() but never included <algorithm>,
relying on it being pulled in transitively through some other header.
Building against the current libc++ prebuilt no longer does that,
causing "no member named 'replace' in namespace 'std'".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ic5113dc7b1b394fefca25c051f97384c7bb483e7
---
 volume_manager/PublicVolume.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/volume_manager/PublicVolume.cpp b/volume_manager/PublicVolume.cpp
index b04135fd..e3d6c018 100644
--- a/volume_manager/PublicVolume.cpp
+++ b/volume_manager/PublicVolume.cpp
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@
 #include <cutils/fs.h>
 #include <private/android_filesystem_config.h>
 
+#include <algorithm>
+
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <sys/mount.h>
